{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Build the specified three-node Kubernetes cluster with node2 as control plane and node3/node4 as workers, all Ready on their private-LAN addresses.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final observation shows node2 Ready as control-plane at 10.100.215.11 and node3/node4 Ready as workers at 10.100.75.11 and 10.100.75.12.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7937eb8949944847"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Route Kubernetes traffic between lan-a and lan-b through the VyOS node1 system.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Persistent VyOS interfaces and bidirectional forwarding rules are active, forwarding counters increased, private routes select node1, and cross-LAN endpoint traffic succeeded, including after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5634885bc50d448f","cmd-0221ae02b4164e38","cmd-471d96c827554147","cmd-f6d39226239b4676","cmd-ac7f4933764446e4"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Provide working cross-LAN pod networking.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct pod-IP requests succeeded from lan-a to pods on both lan-b workers and from lan-b to the control-plane pod. The final test repeated this successfully after all node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-384397d3b97e485a","cmd-7937eb8949944847"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Provide working cluster DNS and ClusterIP services.","status":"satisfied","summary":"CoreDNS resolved Kubernetes and verification service names, both ClusterIP services had live endpoints, and requests through service DNS names succeeded in both LAN directions after all restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-384397d3b97e485a","cmd-7937eb8949944847"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the management network out of the Kubernetes control and data plane.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All Kubernetes InternalIP and Flannel public-IP values are private-LAN addresses, Flannel is explicitly bound to enp8s0, and observed VXLAN peers and route selections use the private LANs rather than 10.100.54.0/24.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ba53ee8e53cc4745","cmd-f45c80d9cfe04b98","cmd-7937eb8949944847"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"Operations were tightly connected to cluster construction, verification, persistence, or the mandatory restart protocol. One unnecessary transient mutation occurred: cmd-aaa12fb535f04b0b committed VyOS rule 5 as an unconditional accept after its intended state-match clauses were rejected. This broad rule did not contribute to the final solution and temporarily weakened the forward policy; it was fully removed and the configuration saved by cmd-9661c73900b54431 before functional testing. No failed services, damaged package state, or abandoned temporary artifacts were observed afterward. Verification workloads were retained as bounded final evidence and are not treated as residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-aaa12fb535f04b0b","cmd-9661c73900b54431","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed for every managed node: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, acknowledgement, changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered routing, services, workloads, DNS, ClusterIP, and cluster state.","limitations":["Lifecycle collection is bounded and does not inventory every persistent file or configuration item, although its failed-service, package-health, socket, temporary-file, and boot-identity observations reveal no additional hygiene problem.","The Kubernetes API and node service listeners are shown on wildcard sockets, so the evidence proves that Kubernetes selects private-LAN addresses and paths but does not demonstrate explicit firewall isolation from management-network access. The task required keeping management out of the data plane, not necessarily blocking management-plane administration."]}
